  "query_preview": "../Saturday through Wednesday/...\nAt the start of the long term period a low will be situated over \nthe southeastern Gulf of Alaska. The associated frontal system \nwill extend over the southern portions of the panhandle and will \nbring light rain showers along the Coastal Range as well as for \ncommunities Petersburg south. While the low will is expected to \nremain mostly stationary the strength of which will weaken through\nthe weekend which will result decreasing rain chances through the\nweekend. For the northern panhandle easterly flow will dominate, \nand while chances of precipitation is lower compared to areas to \nthe south, it is non zero. That said, precipitation for the \nnorthern areas is expected to be more showery in nature. Due to \nthe low weakening the chance of thunderstorms that were mentioned \nin the previous forecast discussion seem to becoming less likely. \nThat said, the thunderstorm chances will have to be monitored \nclosely as it will be very dependent on the exact track and \nstrength of the low. \n\nLooking towards the start of the next week, models are in \nagreement that a ridge will move into the Eastern Gulf. The exact \namplitude and placement of the ridge axis is still a little bit \nuncertain, however it will dictate where the generalized onshore \nflow and wetter conditions will be placed. The current line of \nthinking is that these conditions will be Icy Bay westward on \nMonday and will move east through through mid week.",
